{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N8D2fWgex64pAAgtQrkf6J","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# QuantAgent-3uf — Design: Fix PositionMonitor Unit-Test Regressions\n2\t\n3\t**Issue ID:** QuantAgent-3uf\n4\t**Type:** Bug / Test Infrastructure\n5\t\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t## Context\n9\t\n10\tSee requirements: `docs/01_requirements/QuantAgent-3uf-RQ-fix-positionmonitor-unit-test-regression.md`\n11\t\n12\tThe 4 failing tests are caused by test infrastructure problems, not by bugs in\n13\t`PositionMonitor` business logic. The design changes are minimal and surgical.\n14\t\n15\t---\n16\t\n17\t## Change 1: Remove local `db_session` from both test files\n18\t\n19\t### Problem\n20\t\n21\tBoth test files define a `db_session` fixture locally that wins over the centralized\n22\tone in `conftest.py` whenever `DATABASE_URL` is set:\n23\t\n24\t```python\n25\t# In test_position_monitor.py AND test_position_monitor_constraints.py\n26\t@pytest.fixture\n27\tdef db_session():\n28\t    database_url = os.getenv(\"DATABASE_URL\")\n29\t    if database_url:\n30\t        engine = create_engine(database_url)  # ← uses PostgreSQL in CI\n31\t    else:\n32\t        engine = create_engine(\"sqlite:///:memory:\")\n33\t    Base.metadata.create_all(engine)\n34\t    TestSession = sessionmaker(bind=engine)\n35\t    db = TestSession()\n36\t    yield db\n37\t    db.close()  # ← commits are NOT rolled back; data persists\n38\t```\n39\t\n40\t`conftest.py` already has the correct fixture (added by `QuantAgent-4ch`):\n41\t- Uses SQLite in-memory → function-scoped isolation\n42\t- FK constraints enabled via `PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON`\n43\t- Drops all tables on teardown\n44\t\n45\t### Fix\n46\t\n47\tDelete the entire `db_session` fixture block (fixture + `position_monitor` fixture that\n48\tdepends on it) from both test files. The `conftest.py` fixture will be discovered\n49\tautomatically by pytest.\n50\t\n51\t**Also remove** unused imports: `os`, `create_engine`, `sessionmaker` — these were\n52\tonly used by the local fixture.\n53\t\n54\tNote: The `position_monitor` fixture in both test files creates `PositionMonitor(db_session)`.\n55\tThis does NOT need to change — pytest will inject the `conftest.py` session.\n56\t\n57\tActually the `position_monitor` fixture is local and wraps `db_session` — it must remain.\n58\tOnly the `db_session` definition is removed; the `position_monitor` fixture stays.\n59\t\n60\t### File changes\n61\t\n62\t**`tests/test_position_monitor.py`**: remove lines:\n63\t```python\n64\timport os\n65\t# ...\n66\tfrom sqlalchemy import create_engine\n67\tfrom sqlalchemy.orm import sessionmaker\n68\t# ...\n69\t@pytest.fixture\n70\tdef db_session():\n71\t    \"\"\"Create database session for testing using DATABASE_URL if available.\"\"\"\n72\t    database_url = os.getenv(\"DATABASE_URL\")\n73\t    if database_url:\n74\t        engine = create_engine(database_url)\n75\t    else:\n76\t        # Fallback to SQLite for local development\n77\t        engine = create_engine(\"sqlite:///:memory:\")\n78\t    Base.metadata.create_all(engine)\n79\t    TestSession = sessionmaker(bind=engine)\n80\t    db = TestSession()\n81\t    yield db\n82\t    db.close()\n83\t```\n84\t\n85\tSame removal in **`tests/test_position_monitor_constraints.py`**.\n86\t\n87\t---\n88\t\n89\t## Change 2: Fix FK violation in `test_position_with_all_optional_fields`\n90\t\n91\t### Problem\n92\t\n93\tThe test uses `trade_id=123, signal_id=456` — hardcoded integers that are FKs to\n94\t`trades.id` and `signals.id`. No parent records exist → PostgreSQL raises\n95\t`ForeignKeyViolation`. With SQLite + FK enforcement, this also fails.\n96\t\n97\t### Fix\n98\t\n99\tCreate minimal `Trade` and `Signal` records before opening the position, then use\n100\ttheir auto-assigned IDs. Minimum required fields (non-nullable, no default):\n101\t\n102\t**Trade** (`trades` table):\n103\t- `symbol` (String)\n104\t- `entry_price` (Numeric)\n105\t- `quantity` (Numeric)\n106\t- `side` (Enum OrderSide)\n107\t- `environment` (Enum Environment, default=PAPER)\n108\t- `opened_at` (DateTime, default=utcnow)\n109\t\n110\t**Signal** (`signals` table):\n111\t- `symbol` (String)\n112\t- `signal` (Enum TradeSignal)\n113\t- `confidence` (Float)\n114\t- `timeframe` (String)\n115\t- `environment` (Enum Environment, default=PAPER)\n116\t- `generated_at` (DateTime, default=utcnow)\n117\t\n118\t```python\n119\tdef test_position_with_all_optional_fields(position_monitor, db_session):\n120\t    \"\"\"Validate position creation with all optional fields set.\"\"\"\n121\t    from quantagent.models import Trade, Signal, TradeSignal, OrderSide as OS, Environment\n122\t    from decimal import Decimal as D\n123\t\n124\t    trade = Trade(\n125\t        symbol=\"BTCUSDT\",\n126\t        entry_price=100.0,\n127\t        quantity=D(\"1.0\"),\n128\t        side=OS.BUY,\n129\t    )\n130\t    signal = Signal(\n131\t        symbol=\"BTCUSDT\",\n132\t        signal=TradeSignal.LONG,\n133\t        confidence=0.8,\n134\t        timeframe=\"1h\",\n135\t    )\n136\t    db_session.add_all([trade, signal])\n137\t    db_session.flush()  # populate IDs without committing\n138\t\n139\t    position = position_monitor.open_position(\n140\t        symbol=\"BTCUSDT\",\n141\t        side=OrderSide.BUY,\n142\t        entry_price=100.0,\n143\t        stop_loss=95.0,\n144\t        take_profit=110.0,\n145\t        quantity=Decimal(\"1.0\"),\n146\t        exit_policy=ExitPolicy.TRAILING_STOP,\n147\t        trailing_stop_pct=0.05,\n148\t        max_hold_candles=10,\n149\t        prediction_horizon=5,\n150\t        trade_id=trade.id,\n151\t        signal_id=signal.id,\n152\t    )\n153\t\n154\t    assert position.trailing_stop_pct == 0.05\n155\t    assert position.max_hold_candles == 10\n156\t    assert position.prediction_horizon == 5\n157\t    assert position.trade_id == trade.id\n158\t    assert position.signal_id == signal.id\n159\t```\n160\t\n161\tNote: `db_session.flush()` sends the INSERT to the DB within the current transaction\n162\t(populating auto-increment IDs) without issuing a COMMIT. Since `open_position` then\n163\tdoes its own `db_session.commit()`, all records commit together.\n164\t\n165\t---\n166\t\n167\t## Change 3: Add `ORDER BY` to `get_active_position`\n168\t\n169\t### Problem\n170\t\n171\t`get_active_position` uses `.first()` with no ordering:\n172\t```python\n173\treturn query.first()\n174\t```\n175\t\n176\tIn PostgreSQL and SQLite, without ORDER BY the result is engine-dependent and may vary\n177\tacross runs. When a test directly inserts a second position with the same symbol, which\n178\trecord `.first()` returns is unpredictable.\n179\t\n180\t### Fix\n181\t\n182\tAdd `.order_by(ActivePosition.id)` (ascending) to return the oldest active position\n183\tconsistently:\n184\t\n185\t```python\n186\treturn query.order_by(ActivePosition.id).first()\n187\t```\n188\t\n189\t**Rationale for ASC (oldest first):** The test `test_get_active_position_returns_most_recent_if_multiple`\n190\tasserts `active.id == pos1.id` where pos1 is the first-created position. ASC ordering\n191\tmatches this expectation and is the safest default (if duplicate active positions exist,\n192\tthe system was already in violation; returning the oldest is conservative).\n193\t\n194\tThis is a one-line change in `quantagent/trading/position_monitor.py`.\n195\t\n196\t---\n197\t\n198\t## Non-Changes\n199\t\n200\t- `tests/conftest.py` — no changes (already correct)\n201\t- `quantagent/models.py` — no changes\n202\t- CI workflow — no changes\n203\t- Other test files — no changes\n204\t\n205\t---\n206\t\n207\t## Dependency Chain\n208\t\n209\tChanges are independent. Recommended execution order:\n210\t\n211\t1. Remove local `db_session` from both test files (unblocks 3 of 4 failures)\n212\t2. Fix FK in `test_position_with_all_optional_fields` (fixes 1 remaining failure)\n213\t3. Add `ORDER BY` to `get_active_position` (stabilizes behavior for edge-case test)\n214\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e4119307-b18c-4a04-a8f0-d6dabcd79e06","uuid":"23b40560-7769-405f-bd3e-05efe9d41561","timestamp":"2026-05-08T02:48:26.825Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/docs/03_design/QuantAgent-3uf-DS-fix-positionmonitor-unit-test-regression.md","content":"# QuantAgent-3uf — Design: Fix PositionMonitor Unit-Test Regressions\n\n**Issue ID:** QuantAgent-3uf\n**Type:** Bug / Test Infrastructure\n\n---\n\n## Context\n\nSee requirements: `docs/01_requirements/QuantAgent-3uf-RQ-fix-positionmonitor-unit-test-regression.md`\n\nThe 4 failing tests are caused by test infrastructure problems, not by bugs in\n`PositionMonitor` business logic. The design changes are minimal and surgical.\n\n---\n\n## Change 1: Remove local `db_session` from both test files\n\n### Problem\n\nBoth test files define a `db_session` fixture locally that wins over the centralized\none in `conftest.py` whenever `DATABASE_URL` is set:\n\n```python\n# In test_position_monitor.py AND test_position_monitor_constraints.py\n@pytest.fixture\ndef db_session():\n    database_url = os.getenv(\"DATABASE_URL\")\n    if database_url:\n        engine = create_engine(database_url)  # ← uses PostgreSQL in CI\n    else:\n        engine = create_engine(\"sqlite:///:memory:\")\n    Base.metadata.create_all(engine)\n    TestSession = sessionmaker(bind=engine)\n    db = TestSession()\n    yield db\n    db.close()  # ← commits are NOT rolled back; data persists\n```\n\n`conftest.py` already has the correct fixture (added by `QuantAgent-4ch`):\n- Uses SQLite in-memory → function-scoped isolation\n- FK constraints enabled via `PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON`\n- Drops all tables on teardown\n\n### Fix\n\nDelete the entire `db_session` fixture block (fixture + `position_monitor` fixture that\ndepends on it) from both test files. The `conftest.py` fixture will be discovered\nautomatically by pytest.\n\n**Also remove** unused imports: `os`, `create_engine`, `sessionmaker` — these were\nonly used by the local fixture.\n\nNote: The `position_monitor` fixture in both test files creates `PositionMonitor(db_session)`.\nThis does NOT need to change — pytest will inject the `conftest.py` session.\n\nActually the `position_monitor` fixture is local and wraps `db_session` — it must remain.\nOnly the `db_session` definition is removed; the `position_monitor` fixture stays.\n\n### File changes\n\n**`tests/test_position_monitor.py`**: remove lines:\n```python\nimport os\n# ...\nfrom sqlalchemy import create_engine\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import sessionmaker\n# ...\n@pytest.fixture\ndef db_session():\n    \"\"\"Create database session for testing using DATABASE_URL if available.\"\"\"\n    database_url = os.getenv(\"DATABASE_URL\")\n    if database_url:\n        engine = create_engine(database_url)\n    else:\n        # Fallback to SQLite for local development\n        engine = create_engine(\"sqlite:///:memory:\")\n    Base.metadata.create_all(engine)\n    TestSession = sessionmaker(bind=engine)\n    db = TestSession()\n    yield db\n    db.close()\n```\n\nSame removal in **`tests/test_position_monitor_constraints.py`**.\n\n---\n\n## Change 2: Fix FK violation in `test_position_with_all_optional_fields`\n\n### Problem\n\nThe test uses `trade_id=123, signal_id=456` — hardcoded integers that are FKs to\n`trades.id` and `signals.id`. No parent records exist → PostgreSQL raises\n`ForeignKeyViolation`. With SQLite + FK enforcement, this also fails.\n\n### Fix\n\nCreate minimal `Trade` and `Signal` records before opening the position, then use\ntheir auto-assigned IDs. Minimum required fields (non-nullable, no default):\n\n**Trade** (`trades` table):\n- `symbol` (String)\n- `entry_price` (Numeric)\n- `quantity` (Numeric)\n- `side` (Enum OrderSide)\n- `environment` (Enum Environment, default=PAPER)\n- `opened_at` (DateTime, default=utcnow)\n\n**Signal** (`signals` table):\n- `symbol` (String)\n- `signal` (Enum TradeSignal)\n- `confidence` (Float)\n- `timeframe` (String)\n- `environment` (Enum Environment, default=PAPER)\n- `generated_at` (DateTime, default=utcnow)\n\n```python\ndef test_position_with_all_optional_fields(position_monitor, db_session):\n    \"\"\"Validate position creation with all optional fields set.\"\"\"\n    from quantagent.models import Trade, Signal, TradeSignal, OrderSide as OS, Environment\n    from decimal import Decimal as D\n\n    trade = Trade(\n        symbol=\"BTCUSDT\",\n        entry_price=100.0,\n        quantity=D(\"1.0\"),\n        side=OS.BUY,\n    )\n    signal = Signal(\n        symbol=\"BTCUSDT\",\n        signal=TradeSignal.LONG,\n        confidence=0.8,\n        timeframe=\"1h\",\n    )\n    db_session.add_all([trade, signal])\n    db_session.flush()  # populate IDs without committing\n\n    position = position_monitor.open_position(\n        symbol=\"BTCUSDT\",\n        side=OrderSide.BUY,\n        entry_price=100.0,\n        stop_loss=95.0,\n        take_profit=110.0,\n        quantity=Decimal(\"1.0\"),\n        exit_policy=ExitPolicy.TRAILING_STOP,\n        trailing_stop_pct=0.05,\n        max_hold_candles=10,\n        prediction_horizon=5,\n        trade_id=trade.id,\n        signal_id=signal.id,\n    )\n\n    assert position.trailing_stop_pct == 0.05\n    assert position.max_hold_candles == 10\n    assert position.prediction_horizon == 5\n    assert position.trade_id == trade.id\n    assert position.signal_id == signal.id\n```\n\nNote: `db_session.flush()` sends the INSERT to the DB within the current transaction\n(populating auto-increment IDs) without issuing a COMMIT. Since `open_position` then\ndoes its own `db_session.commit()`, all records commit together.\n\n---\n\n## Change 3: Add `ORDER BY` to `get_active_position`\n\n### Problem\n\n`get_active_position` uses `.first()` with no ordering:\n```python\nreturn query.first()\n```\n\nIn PostgreSQL and SQLite, without ORDER BY the result is engine-dependent and may vary\nacross runs. When a test directly inserts a second position with the same symbol, which\nrecord `.first()` returns is unpredictable.\n\n### Fix\n\nAdd `.order_by(ActivePosition.id)` (ascending) to return the oldest active position\nconsistently:\n\n```python\nreturn query.order_by(ActivePosition.id).first()\n```\n\n**Rationale for ASC (oldest first):** The test `test_get_active_position_returns_most_recent_if_multiple`\nasserts `active.id == pos1.id` where pos1 is the first-created position. ASC ordering\nmatches this expectation and is the safest default (if duplicate active positions exist,\nthe system was already in violation; returning the oldest is conservative).\n\nThis is a one-line change in `quantagent/trading/position_monitor.py`.\n\n---\n\n## Non-Changes\n\n- `tests/conftest.py` — no changes (already correct)\n- `quantagent/models.py` — no changes\n- CI workflow — no changes\n- Other test files — no changes\n\n---\n\n## Dependency Chain\n\nChanges are independent. Recommended execution order:\n\n1. Remove local `db_session` from both test files (unblocks 3 of 4 failures)\n2. Fix FK in `test_position_with_all_optional_fields` (fixes 1 remaining failure)\n3. Add `ORDER BY` to `get_active_position` (stabilizes behavior for edge-case test)\n","numLines":214,"startLine":1,"totalLines":214}}}
